# What Vercel uploads = the app, not the workshop around it.
#
# The working branch carries the test suites, the static GitHub Pages export,
# the design notes and the hand-off files. None of that belongs in a deployment:
# it is uploaded, built and then paid for in build minutes, and it is the only
# real difference between "the files we work on" and "the files that go live".
# Keeping one branch and excluding the rest here means the two can never drift.

# Test suites and their helpers
qa/

# GitHub Pages static export + its redirect page
docs/
index.html

# Notes, plans, hand-off scripts
*.md
deprecated/
publish-final.sh
final-site.tar.gz
realign.sh

# Local state and secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.pglite/
.pgdata/
out/
.next/
node_modules/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Screenshots and session artefacts
.arena/
shots/
verify/
verify-*.png
